.TH QFW_CHEM_APP.SH 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Examples"
.SH NAME
qfw_chem_app.sh \- run a QFw-enabled chemistry application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_chem_app.sh [common-options] [--chem-app-dir directory] \e
  script.py [script-arguments ...]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw_chem_app.sh
locates an external chemistry application, starts or connects to the selected
QPM, and launches the script through
.BR qfw-srun (1).
The wrapper appends
.B --qfw
and
.BI --backend " name"
to the application arguments. The selected script must implement those
options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --chem-app-dir " directory"
Directory containing the chemistry script. If omitted, the wrapper checks the
adjacent
.I chemistry_example_aim2
checkout and the installed example test tree.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command help.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --service-mode " mode"
Use application-owned
.B local
services or an existing
.B site
QPM. The default is local.
.TP
.BI --backend " name"
Select the QPM provider. The default comes from
.B QFW_CHEM_BACKEND
or falls back to
.BR nwqsim .
.TP
.BI --site-config " path"
Override the activated site configuration.
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " path"
Override the installed runtime selected by the service mode.
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable shell tracing.
.PP
Common options must precede
.B --chem-app-dir
and the script name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QFW_CHEM_APP_DIR
Default chemistry application directory.
.TP
.B QFW_CHEM_BACKEND
Default backend when
.B --backend
is omitted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the AIM2 helium smoke input on an application-owned NWQSim QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_chem_app.sh --service-mode local --backend nwqsim \e
  --chem-app-dir /path/to/chemistry_example_aim2 \e
  example_1_He_from_pyscf.py --smoke --no-draw \e
  --reservation-shots 16
.EE
.PP
Run the same bounded input through a site-owned IQM QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_chem_app.sh --service-mode site --backend iqm \e
  --chem-app-dir /path/to/chemistry_example_aim2 \e
  example_1_He_from_pyscf.py --smoke --no-draw \e
  --reservation-shots 16
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw_run_all.sh (1),
.BR qfw-examples (7),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw-runtime.yaml (5)
